\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Walk-forward estimation over six consecutive decision dates. Each row represents the portfolio decision at the indicated day's close, marked by the vertical gray line. Blue bars identify the observations used by the active PCA estimate, and green bars identify the regression window. In this example, PCA refits at \(t\) and \(t+3\), so its estimation window remains unchanged for three rows before advancing. The regression refits daily using the active PCA weights, including a new factor basis when PCA updates. Orange bars show the subsequent return interval earned by the chosen portfolio. Estimation periods lie entirely before or at the decision close, while portfolio returns occur afterward. Window lengths and the three-day PCA interval are illustrative rather than strategy defaults.\relax }}{6}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:framework-walkforward}{{7}{6}{Walk-forward estimation over six consecutive decision dates. Each row represents the portfolio decision at the indicated day's close, marked by the vertical gray line. Blue bars identify the observations used by the active PCA estimate, and green bars identify the regression window. In this example, PCA refits at \(t\) and \(t+3\), so its estimation window remains unchanged for three rows before advancing. The regression refits daily using the active PCA weights, including a new factor basis when PCA updates. Orange bars show the subsequent return interval earned by the chosen portfolio. Estimation periods lie entirely before or at the decision close, while portfolio returns occur afterward. Window lengths and the three-day PCA interval are illustrative rather than strategy defaults.\relax }{figure.caption.19}{}}
